        // The rule: if atVersion does not revert, then the controller address must be the real one (not the buggy one)
        // The bug changes controller() to return a dead address, so any successful atVersion call would use a wrong oracle
        // But we need a more general rule: the controller address returned must be a contract with code
        if (!reverted) {
